SUMMARY:16 Volt + Acumen Nation
DTSTART;TZID=US/Pacific:20260909T190000
DURATION:PT4H
URL:https://www.dnalounge.com/calendar/2026/09-09d.html
X-THUMBNAIL:https://www.dnalounge.com/flyers/2026/09/09d.html
DESCRIPTION;ALTREP="https://www.dnalounge.com/calendar/2026/09-09d.html":
 Performing Live:\n\n
   16 VOLT\n
   ACUMEN NATION\n
   EVERYTHING GOES COLD\n\n
 With DJ:\n\n
   Starr Noir\n\n
 As a celebration of the 30-Year anniversary of 16 Volt's \"Let Down
  Crush\" and Acumen's \"Territory = Universe\" these Cold Wave icons
  will be performing special album-focused sets in a rare return to the
  Bay Area.\n\n
 16volt's founder\, songwriter\, lead vocalist\, programmer\, and
  rhythm guitarist\, Eric Powell\, signed his first record deal in 1991
  at a very young age and subsequently released three albums: including
  the legendary LetDownCrush in 1996\, to widespread acclaim and
  notoriety. With its roots originally planted firmly in the industrial
  rock genre\, 16 Volt have remained a mainstay enjoying a worldwide
  underground fanbase and successfully crossing over into genres for
  decades.\n\n
 Acumen Nation is an American industrial rock and coldwave band formed
  in Chicago in 1988. Known for blending heavy metal guitars with
  pulsating electronic beats\, they were founded by brothers Jason and
  Ethan Novak. They are widely recognized as stalwarts of the Midwest
  underground industrial scene. Their landmark album \"Territory =
  Universe\" is celebrated for its dense\, layered production and heavy
  guitar-driven electronic sound\n\n
 Everything Goes Cold forcibly and indignantly amalgamates influences
  from the full spectrum of classic American guitar-based industrial
  music with a modern sensibility and foul attitude that makes the lead
  singer of your favorite terror Ebm band look and smell like your
  great-grandfather after a long day in the sun. Everything Goes Cold
  will freeze you to death and tear your face off. Maybe they already
  have. We're fairly certain you had more face before\, and you should
  probably put on a coat.\n\n
 industrial. cold wave.\n
 doors @ 7pm\;\n
 show @ 7:30pm.\n
 all ages.\n
 $22 limited advance\;\n
 $31 after\;\n
 $31 day of show.\n\n
 Buy tickets: https://www.dnalounge.com/calendar/2026/09-09d.html\n\n
 Watch and listen:\n
   16 Volt: The Last Time: https://youtu.be/ivvOwFwWdUg\n
   Everything Goes Cold: Nadir: https://youtu.be/e5q_Y3HJ76k
CLASS:PUBLIC
CATEGORIES:Performance
STATUS:CONFIRMED
